1339
Descendant selection names the one lineage source for an exact member pause: the grant binds the
queue row's root_task_id (what assignment rechecks), and request_pause resolves one tree for its seed
launch lock and durable row (explicit root verbatim, else from task_metadata like member_fence); without
it a member's Resume is granted under itself and revoked as root_resume_generation_stale. The Owner
Pause paragraph states that restore raises an owner marker's latch from its queue root's durable fence,
so a restart never revives a released owner Pause nor overwrites a newer one. The same paragraph names
the one selection predicate assignment and reserve_attempt share, so an owner-Resumed child of a
monetary latch reaches its sends while siblings, the unselected root and re-paused rows stay fenced,
and which root pause opens a new latch; the restart row states that a stop or restore raises a latch
with the live generation rule for a pause the snapshot map never saw, otherwise its latches stand, and unknown owner
authority keeps the map's latch.
The selection sentence adds the launch handoff (a readiness wake never starts under a monetary latch),
and the sleep-clock paragraph says cold consumption retires only sleep_exclusion_since, keeping an
explicit Resume's fence-bound selection; pending timing, not carrier presence, is what a warm park reconciles.
